{
  "inShort": "The checkpoint is at risk: the opened evidence does not establish a playable slice. Four reference and setup tasks closed, but the devlog’s tide and co-op claims remain unverified. Neither a second island nor five-player testing was shown.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x0600jscsz8r4935jty",
      "text": "The public Godot repository matches the task, including demo folders and import instructions. It supplies a starting point, not evidence of this game’s implementation."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x0s00jtcsz8az0lkwpy",
      "text": "The task is closed with an art reference. The inspected title and thumbnail identify Big Buck Bunny, not game footage. The video was not watched, so its animation cannot be assessed. A chosen game style remains unproven."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x1800jucsz8wothj7j8",
      "text": "The Wikipedia article matches the promised playtesting reference. It supports test preparation but does not show that players tested the slice."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvun2x1q00jvcsz8qpwzz58f",
      "text": "The private design board closes the setup task. No board contents were supplied for review, so it provides no visible evidence of design decisions."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [
    "cmvun2x2600jwcsz8e6von2yr"
  ],
  "outsidePlan": [],
  "questions": [
    "What playable evidence supports the reported tide loop and two-player sailing?",
    "How do the remaining tasks account for the second island and five-player test?",
    "Which visual reference has the team chosen as the game’s style?"
  ],
  "lenses": {
    "marketing": "Devlog #1 reported tide and co-op progress, but showed a landscape photograph and a Big Buck Bunny reference; it received 0 applause and 0 views, and no game page is listed.",
    "team": "Only Alex’s 40–60 checkpoint hours are quantified, leaving Mia’s contribution outside the capacity estimate. Both are listed as newly joined and confirmed working, giving the tasks engineering coverage, but one sprint cannot establish pace.",
    "management": "Four setup tasks closed, but the remaining trailer storyboard does not account for the playable slice within 28 days. The public prototype devlog meets the listed stage publication requirement, while the proven core and chosen style remain unestablished."
  }
}

